1. CHECK GIT VERSION
Command:
git --version

Purpose:
To check whether Git is installed.


2. CREATE A NEW FOLDER
Command:
mkdir GitExperiment1

Purpose:
To create a folder named GitExperiment1.


3. OPEN THE FOLDER
Command:
cd GitExperiment1

Purpose:
To enter the GitExperiment1 folder.


4. CREATE A TEXT FILE
Command:
echo Student Details > Student.txt

Purpose:
To create Student.txt and write Student Details inside it.


5. INITIALIZE GIT REPOSITORY
Command:
git init

Purpose:
To initialize Git in the current folder.


6. CHECK REPOSITORY STATUS
Command:
git status

Purpose:
To check the current status of files.


7. ADD A FILE TO THE STAGING AREA
Command:
git add Student.txt

Purpose:
To prepare Student.txt for committing.


8. ADD ALL FILES TO THE STAGING AREA
Command:
git add .

Purpose:
To prepare all files for committing.


9. COMMIT THE FILE
Command:
git commit -m "Add student details"

Purpose:
To save the staged changes in Git history.


10. RENAME THE BRANCH TO MAIN
Command:
git branch -M main

Purpose:
To rename the current branch to main.


11. CONNECT THE LOCAL REPOSITORY TO GITHUB
Command:
git remote add origin https://github.com/sivapriyakumar246-cyber/GitExperiment1.git

Purpose:
To connect the local repository to the GitHub repository.


12. CHECK THE REMOTE REPOSITORY
Command:
git remote -v

Purpose:
To display the connected remote repository URL.


13. UPLOAD FILES TO GITHUB
Command:
git push -u origin main

Purpose:
To upload committed files to GitHub.


14. DOWNLOAD UPDATES FROM GITHUB
Command:
git pull origin main

Purpose:
To download and integrate changes from GitHub.


15. MERGE UNRELATED REPOSITORY HISTORIES
Command:
git pull origin main --allow-unrelated-histories

Purpose:
To combine two repositories that have separate histories.

Note:
Use this only when necessary.


16. DISPLAY COMMIT HISTORY
Command:
git log --oneline

Purpose:
To display the commit history.


17. DISPLAY FILES IN THE CURRENT FOLDER
Command:
dir

Purpose:
To list the files and folders.


18. DISPLAY TEXT FILE CONTENTS
Command:
type Student.txt

Purpose:
To display the contents of Student.txt.


19. CHECK THE CURRENT BRANCH
Command:
git branch

Purpose:
To display the available local branches.


20. CREATE ANOTHER FILE
Command:
echo Hello GitHub > hello.txt

Purpose:
To create hello.txt with the text Hello GitHub.


21. ADD THE NEW FILE
Command:
git add hello.txt

Purpose:
To prepare hello.txt for committing.


22. COMMIT THE NEW FILE
Command:
git commit -m "Add hello file"

Purpose:
To save the new file in Git history.


23. PUSH NEW CHANGES TO GITHUB
Command:
git push

Purpose:
To upload new committed changes to GitHub.


24. CLONE A GITHUB REPOSITORY
Command:
git clone https://github.com/sivapriyakumar246-cyber/GitExperiment1.git

Purpose:
To download a copy of a GitHub repository.


25. VIEW COMMIT DETAILS
Command:
git log

Purpose:
To display detailed commit history.


26. CHECK UNCOMMITTED CHANGES
Command:
git diff

Purpose:
To display changes that have not been staged.


27. REMOVE A FILE FROM GIT
Command:
git rm hello.txt

Purpose:
To stage the removal of hello.txt from Git.


28. COMMIT FILE REMOVAL
Command:
git commit -m "Remove hello file"

Purpose:
To save the file removal in Git history.


29. CHECK REMOTE DETAILS
Command:
git remote show origin

Purpose:
To display information about the remote repository.


30. FINAL STATUS CHECK
Command:
git status

Purpose:
To check whether all changes have been committed.

